# 72: an alias reached through a ROOT-SPLICED include leaves a `must()`
# written at the use site unresolved, and only in TypeScript.
#
# The schema half declares `%Cents` and spreads a `type(close({...}))`
# over `lines`; this file splices it and adds one member whose
# `amountCents` carries a `must()`.
#
# run: node ../../../ts/bin/aontu.js spliced-alias-strands-a-must.aon
# run: aontu-go spliced-alias-strands-a-must.aon
#
# expected (and what Go answers, exit 0):
#   {"lines":{"one":{"amountCents":10,"unitCents":10}},"schema":{}}
#
# actual, TypeScript, exit 1:
#   [aontu/mapval_required]: Cannot resolve value at path
#   $.lines.one.amountCents
#    Cannot resolve value: 10&must(.unitCents,"no")
#
# THREE THINGS ARE NEEDED and dropping any one of them makes it pass in
# both ports: the alias (write `integer & min(0)` at both use sites and
# it resolves), the ROOT SPLICE (put the two files' contents in one
# file and it resolves), and the `must()` at the use site (`max(99)`
# there, or nothing, resolves). So it is the alias reference surviving
# the splice into the spread template that leaves the relative-argument
# constraint a round short of settling.

@"./spliced-alias-strands-a-must-schema.aon"

lines: {
  one: { unitCents: 10, amountCents: 10 & must(.unitCents, "no") }
}
